course: dictionary
lesson: 4315
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The same piece has three names: a meteoroid in space, a meteor while it glows in the air, and a meteorite if any of it lands on the ground.» Here ground means the surface of the Earth that you stand on, because something has landed on it.
explain: Ground can also mean soil, the earth that plants grow in. In Ukraine, «steppe grass roots dying and rotting into the ground» built up black earth over thousands of years, so ground here means soil. Ask yourself: does this meaning fit the sentence? If it does, you have found it.
explain: «Playground» is a word made from ground. A playground is an area of land used for play, so the word ground can mean a piece of land used for something. When a word is hard to pin down, swap in a simple meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Ground is a noun (ground, grounds) and a verb (ground, grounds, grounded).
fact: As a noun, ground can mean the surface of the Earth, soil or earth, or an area of land used for something, like a playground or a sports ground.
fact: As a verb, ground means to keep a child at home as punishment, or to keep a plane from flying.
fact: Ground is also the past of grind, as in ground coffee.
fact: Phrases with ground include on the ground, ground floor, underground and stand your ground.
exercise: «The same piece has three names: a meteoroid in space, a meteor while it glows in the air, and a meteorite if any of it lands on the ground.» What does ground mean here? | A reason for doing something | The past of grind | A playing field with goals | * The surface of the Earth that you stand on
exercise: Ella's mum says she will ground her for a week. What does ground mean here? | To make her very tired | To grind her food into powder | To dig a hole in the soil | * To keep her at home as punishment
exercise: «Vervet monkeys stand and look at the ground when they hear the snake call.» What is the ground in this sentence? | * Soil and earth | An area used for sport | The past of grind | A reason
exercise: Which word is the past of grind? | grinds | * ground | grounded | grinding
test: «The children ran around the playground.» What does playground mean? | A reason for a game | A kind of soil | The surface of the sea | * An area of land used for play
test: Which sentence uses ground as a verb? | The meteorite hit the ground. | * The pilot's plane was grounded because of the fog. | Ostriches lie flat with their necks along the ground. | The ground coffee smelled lovely.
exam: «Ukraine's black earth was built over thousands of years by steppe grass roots dying and rotting into the ground.» In this sentence, what does ground mean? | A sports field | * Soil and earth | A reason for something | The past of grind
